{"name":"Begonia","hex":"#fa6e79","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Begonia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Begoniaceae – begonias, native to many tropical and subtropical environments and grown as houseplants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Begonia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Begonia","blocks":[{"text":"Begonia is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Begoniaceae. The genus contains more than 2,000 different plant species, distributed primarily across tropical and subtropical regions of Africa, Asia, and Central and South America, with Africa considered the center of origin. Some species are commonly grown indoors as ornamental houseplants in cooler climates, or cultivated outside in summertime for their bright colorful flowers, which have petals but no sepals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Begonia_obliqua00.jpg/330px-Begonia_obliqua00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Begonia","wikidata":"Q158617"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Petals_0016.jpg/500px-Petals_0016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Petals_0016.jpg/1280px-Petals_0016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Petals_0016.jpg/500px-Petals_0016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink flowering Begonia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APetals_0016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/BegoniaBrevirimosa.jpg/120px-BegoniaBrevirimosa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c